nt=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br />Pressure increased from 1 atm to P atm<br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></math> is -ve, so melting in forward direction spontaneous.<br /><br />&nbsp; Method 2 :<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mi>I</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>e</mi><mover> <mo>&#8652;</mo> <mrow></mrow> </mover> <mi>W</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi> </mrow> </math><br /><br />On Increasing P : Molecule&nbsp;&nbsp;<br. br=\"\">Come closer &amp; density increasing; water is formed;<br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Ice &rarr; Water;<br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Since&nbsp; <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>S</mi> <mrow> <mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>e</mi> </mrow> </msub> <mo>&#60;</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><msub> <mi>S</mi> <mrow> <mi>w</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi> </mrow></msub></mrow></math></br.><br /><br />&nbsp;<math> <mo>&#8757;Process From Ice to water is spontaneous;</mo></math><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mi>&#916;</mi><mi>G</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn> </mrow> </math></p><p>In physical equilibrium, on increasing pressure, equilibrium shift toward more density side.</p>",
